Subject: [PATCH] redact: a host's name goes as one under .example the agent
 can use
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Told "ssh to {{HOSTNAME_…}}", the model asked the user for the real host
instead of running ssh, as it did for an address before its
documentation one (#4063). A host's name the user@host rules find (a
shell prompt's, an ssh command's, a HostName or hostname line's) now
goes as one under the .example set aside for it (RFC 2606's), made from
the host as a user name's stand-in is (hostStandInOf), so it is the same
every turn and a vendor's cache still matches. No one's host ends in
.example (hostOK never masks one), so a stand-in is never taken for a
host the user wrote, and it never masks again. It is put back only
where it stands as a whole name, in a streamed tool call's arguments
too (restoreHost): sub.qmvkrta.example and qmvkrta.example.net are no
put-back of qmvkrta.example, a full stop with none of a name's bytes
after it ends the sentence and the name under it is put back. Preview
shows the same stand-in.

Run:
- New tests (internal/redact/standin_host_test.go): an ssh command's
  host under .example with no placeholder, the same stand-in twice, the
  preview the same, the reply and the tool call put back whole and
  streamed cut at every byte, whole-name boundaries (a port, a sentence
  full stop, brackets against sub., .net, .5, a letter and a digit
  beside it), a stand-in never masked again, and the other host rules
  (Hostname:, ssh config's HostName, a prompt) the same way.
  TestMoreKinds wants the stand-in now.
- Broken by hand: without hostStandIn (shape.go and redact.go's Preview
  back at f982e46f2, the new test kept) TestHostGoesAsAStandInUnderExample
  is red: sent "run ssh cfpvdwbw@{{HOSTNAME_fszqay2y}} -p 22 …", want
  the host under .example; TestOtherHostRulesGoAsAStandIn is red on all
  three rules. With the change back: ok.

